#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/maas/maas.rst:2
msgid "Canonical MAAS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/maas/maas.rst:4
msgid ""
"MAAS from Canonical is an open-source server orchestration tool. It's "
"designed to allow administrators to build a datacenter from on-premises, "
"bare-metal servers where large networks of individual units can be "
"discovered, deployed, and reconfigured."
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/maas/maas.rst:7
msgid "Integrating MAAS and |morpheus|"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/maas/maas.rst:9
msgid ""
"Integrating MAAS with |morpheus| is a simple process requiring the MAAS "
"API URL and API Key. We'll start by gathering what we need from the MAAS "
"UI, then move back into |morpheus| to store the required details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/maas/maas.rst:11
msgid ""
"We can gather the API key by clicking on the username in the upper-right "
"corner of the MAAS UI window. From this preferences page, click on \"API "
"keys\" as shown in the screenshot:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/maas/maas.rst:13
msgid ".. image:: /images/integration_guides/clouds/maas/1prefPage.png"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/maas/maas.rst:15
msgid ""
"From the API keys page, select the displayed key and copy it. "
"Alternatively, you can click the copy button in the UI to add the full "
"key to your clipboard. Store this key in an accessible location for a "
"later step."
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/maas/maas.rst:17
msgid ".. image:: /images/integration_guides/clouds/maas/2maasApi.png"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/maas/maas.rst:19
msgid ""
"In addition to the API key, we need the MAAS API URL. As entered in "
"|morpheus|, the value will be like the following example: ``http://<maas-"
"hostname-or-ip>:5240``. We'll enter the API URL into |morpheus| duriong "
"the next step."
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/maas/maas.rst:21
msgid ""
"In |morpheus|, navigate to the list of integrated Clouds and start a new "
"MAAS Cloud integration:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/maas/maas.rst:23
msgid "Infrastructure > Clouds"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/maas/maas.rst:24
msgid "Click :guilabel:`+ ADD`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/maas/maas.rst:25
msgid "Select \"MAAS\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/maas/maas.rst:26
msgid "Click :guilabel:`NEXT`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/maas/maas.rst:28
msgid ""
"On the \"CREATE CLOUD\" modal, you must at least give a friendly name for"
" the Cloud in |morpheus|, MAAS API URL and API KEY. An example is shown "
"below:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/maas/maas.rst:30
msgid ".. image:: /images/integration_guides/clouds/maas/3createCloud.png"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/maas/maas.rst:33
msgid "Tip"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/maas/maas.rst:33
msgid ""
"You'll know the credentials are entered correctly when your list of MAAS "
"resource pools is synced in as you can see in the example screenshot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/maas/maas.rst:35
msgid ""
"Click :guilabel:`NEXT` and add this new Cloud to an existing Group or "
"create a new Group for it. Once you advanced past the end of the wizard, "
"the Cloud is added and |morpheus| begins to inventory (if you've opted to"
" inventory when adding the Cloud)."
msgstr ""

